Each box is chosen with probability $\frac{1}{3}$. The chance of drawing white is $1$ from the all-white box, $\frac{1}{2}$ from the mixed box, and $0$ from the all-black box.

The weights on a white ball are $\frac{1}{3} \cdot 1 = \frac{1}{3}$ and $\frac{1}{3} \cdot \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{6}$, totalling $\frac{1}{2}$.

P(\text{all-white} \mid \text{white}) = \frac{1/3}{1/2} = \frac{2}{3}
